Part 3: Big-O Notation
===============================
Big-O tells us how an algorithm grows as the input size increases.

Common complexities:

Complexity	Meaning	    Good?
O(1)	      Constant	  ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
O(log n)	Logarithmic  	⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
O(n)	      Linear	    ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
O(n log n)	Sorting	    ⭐⭐⭐⭐
O(n²)	      Nested loops	⭐⭐
O(2ⁿ)     	Exponential	     ❌
O(n!)	        Factorial   	❌

Example 1
print(nums[0])

Time:

O(1)

No matter if the array has 10 or 1 million elements, it takes constant time.


Example 2
for num in nums:
    print(num)

If the array has:

10 elements → 10 operations
100 elements → 100 operations
1000 elements → 1000 operations
Complexity:

O(n)


Example 3
for i in nums:
    for j in nums:
        print(i, j)

Operations:

n × n

Complexity:

O(n²)


